  "instructions_for_next_hop": "Increment 'hop' by 1. Replace 'text' with the next ~250-word installment of the story (keep 'text' around 250 words total, updating 'summary_so_far' and 'story_bible' to retain memory across the 100 hops). Output ONLY valid JSON.",
  "text": "The iron hatch rang like a struck gong. Mara braced her boots against the narrow grating as the sonar pulse bled through the riveted plates, leaving a metallic taste on her tongue. Below them, the hollow core of Spire Four dropped away into a roaring, steam-choked dark.\n\nBeside her, Kael slumped against the curving wall, his breath shallow and wet. In the faint, phosphorescent glow of the lichen coating the shaft, his lips were the color of bruised lead. The sixty-two-pin wheel in his sternum had stalled entirely against the jammed mainspring shard.\n\n\"Wait,\" Mara whispered. Outside, the muffled thrash of the Registry cutter’s propeller passed directly beside the spire, its wash slapping the iron shell. Slowly, the churning faded into the fog, following the drift of the sinking skiff’s air bubbles.\n\nThe moment the sound receded, Mara gripped the slick bronze shard protruding from Kael’s chest and yanked it free.\n\n*Clack-tock. Clack-tock. Clack-tock.*\n\nThe escapement caught with a violent shudder. Kael gasped, arching his back as the brass teeth bit into their rhythm, spraying a fine mist of blood and warm oil across Mara’s knuckles. Within the cylindrical stone chimney, the sound was no longer a whisper; the shaft acted as an organ pipe, amplifying his heartbeat into a deep, resonant percussion that echoed down into the abyss.\n\n\"Down,\" Kael rasped, wiping his mouth with the back of his caliper-splinted hand. \"The water level inside the shaft is equalized to the sub-basin. If we don't get below the limestone shelf before they circle back, the stone itself will carry the beat to their hulls.\"\n\nMara adjusted the lead ledger’s strap across her chest and swung her legs over the lip onto the vertical bronze ladder."
