  "summary_so_far": "Hops 1-5: As an early, coppery tide floods the Grey Flats, Mara salvages an ancient bronze diving bell ('ARCHIVE ZERO') in her nets. Melting its seal shatters her grandfather's tide-clock mainspring. Inside is a boy with brass calipers splinted to his fingers and a lead ledger. He hands her a hot 62-pin escapement wheel, warns that 'The Registry dropped the third weight,' and collapses.\nHops 6-10: Mara uses the boy's calipers to open the ledger ('400 FATHOMS BELOW DATUM'), learning the Flats sit over an abyss. When the clockwork in his chest stops, she inserts the 62-pin gear into his sternum, reviving him. Kael wakes, warning his ticking chest is a beacon for the Registry. Taking her grandfather's clock arbor and broken mainspring, they flee in her skiff as the bell drags her stilts-house under.\nHops 11-16: At Spire Four, Kael muffles his chest with a mainspring shard. They unlock the spire and descend twenty fathoms to the Sluice-Gallery, finding the counterweight chain and drop-cage brake severed by a thermal-lance. Mara rigs her grandfather's mainspring into the cable sleeve as a friction-brake, and they drop into the moon pool.\nHops 17-20: Registry acoustic mines sever the upper cable at 150 fathoms. Kael slams the brake, welding the mainspring to the lower sea-floor cable. Slowing past 310 fathoms, they enter a warm amber glow and see the Illuminated Weir at 390 fathoms—a vast dome crushed by the fallen Third Counterweight. Their cage slams onto the counterweight and tips against the dome.\nHops 21-22: Pinned over a pocket of hyper-compressed air trapped in the dome's crown, Kael unscrews the cage's floor-lens. Fifty atmospheres of air blast the quartz inward, equalizing the cage. They scramble onto the catwalk just as the cage slips off, leaving the broken pane to vent their air bubble into the sea.\nHop 23: Moving through air as thick as syrup while the black water floor rises toward the catwalk, they sprint to the central cylindrical