  "instructions_for_next_hop": "Increment 'hop' by 1. Replace 'text' with the next ~250-word installment of the story (keep 'text' around 250 words total, updating 'summary_so_far' and 'story_bible' to retain memory across the 100 hops). Output ONLY valid JSON.",
  "text": "The stench of scorching leather filled the aisle as the overhead drive-belt shrieked against the stalled pulley. Kael’s jaw clenched, veins standing out dark against his salt-pale neck as the feeder-cam ground into the brass splints on his fingers. Every three seconds, the vermilion Red-Line tube hissed again, slamming another surge of surface air against the piston, driving the steel teeth deeper into the soft brass.\n\nMara dropped the lead ledger onto the grating and snatched the six-inch shard of her grandfather’s tempered steel mainspring from Kael’s belt. She didn't aim for the wire first. Instead, she shoved the blue-steel ribbon directly under the cam’s pawl, right beside Kael’s mangled calipers.\n\nThe next pneumatic pulse hit. The iron pawl struck the clock-spring, couldn't bite through the high-carbon steel, and kicked back with a deafening *crack* that sheared the feeder-pin clean off. \n\nThe overhead belt snapped with a sound like a rifle shot, whipping harmlessly into the rafters. Kael wrenched his hand free, cradling his bleeding fingers against his ticking sternum. The Vernier scales were bent at a jagged angle, scored deep by the loom's teeth.\n\nBreathing hard, the camphor-frost stinging her throat, Mara sawed the sharp edge of the mainspring shard across the braided wire loop. The wire parted. She caught the last three phosphor-bronze plates before they could slide into the guillotine’s throat.\n\nBefore she could lift them to the bioluminescent lamp, a hollow *thump* echoed from the brass dispatch cylinder mounted beside the vermilion air-hose. A heavy leather-padded canister had just dropped four hundred fathoms down the pneumatic return tube from the surface."
