  "text": "The descent was a blind plummet through warm, rancid spermaceti fog. The cast-iron rings of the tube flashed past like the ribs of a leviathan, lit only by the orange sparks screaming off Kael’s leather braking-glove as he feathered the hand-lever.\n\nParallel to their cable, bolted to the sweating iron wall, ran two things: a massive link-chain as thick as Mara’s waist, frozen taut under unbearable tension, and a canvas-wrapped rubber hose the thickness of a man’s wrist. Every ten seconds, the hose twitched—a feeble, stuttering pulse.\n\n\"Vesper’s air-umbilical,\" Mara shouted over the shrill whine of the sheaves, her voice squeaking like a mouse’s in the dense gas. \"The auxiliary pump is barely turning!\"\n\n\"The main drive-chain is taking the whole load of the jammed counterweight above us,\" Kael piped back, his shoulder blades working against her chest as he leaned on the iron brake-handle. \"If a link shears before we trip the bypass valves at five hundred, the recoil will whip through this shaft and cut us in half.\"\n\nAt four hundred and fifty fathoms, the iron tube opened out as if they had exited the throat of a bell into its flare. Below them, swimming in a haze of vaporized oil and phosphorus lamps, lay a subterranean sea of boiling mercury—and rising from its mirror-bright surface, the bronze scaffolding of the Abyssal Tide-Engine.\n\nMara stared down past Kael's salt-white hair. She knew that silhouette. Her grandfather hadn't just stolen a single 62-pin wheel from Archive Zero; he had modeled her entire childhood house upon this engine."
