  "instructions_for_next_hop": "Increment 'hop' by 1. Replace 'text' with the next ~250-word installment of the story (keep 'text' around 250 words total, updating 'summary_so_far' and 'story_bible' to retain memory across the 100 hops). Output ONLY valid JSON.",
  "text": "The bosun’s chair kissed the perforated iron catwalk with a dull clang. Around them, the cavern walls wept black brine that hissed as it struck the pool of heated quicksilver below. The mercury didn’t boil from fire; it shivered with the low, sub-audible vibration of a million tons of sea-water pressing against the bedrock roof, acting as a frictionless float-bath for the bronze colossus rising from its center.\n\n\"Four stilts,\" Mara whispered, her helium-thinned voice trembling as she stepped off the chair. Four monumental fluted columns of green-patinated brass rose from cast-iron pontoons floating on the silver mirror. Between them hung the great horizontal gear-trains, arranged in the exact layout of the rooms she had slept, cooked, and cataloged books in for twenty years. The kitchen hearth was the mainratchet; her bedroom alcove was the pallet-bridge.\n\n\"Your grandfather was First Artificer here before he fled to the surface,\" Kael said, unstrapping the three phosphor-bronze plates from his back. His chest ticked rapidly—*clack-clack-clack*—straining against his ribs as if the 62-pin wheel inside him felt the magnetic pull of the stalled engine. \"He built your house as a one-tenth scale working model so you wouldn't forget the geometry.\"\n\nAbove them, a gunshot crack echoed down the Sump-Well. Flakes of rust snowed onto the mercury. One of the outer plates of the great drive-chain had just split under the weight of the jammed Third Counterweight.\n\nnext to the catwalk, Vesper’s rubber air-umbilical gave a half-hearted spasm and went completely flat.\n\n\"He's out of air,\" Kael said, stepping toward the central altar where the Zero-Spindle waited—a hollow, three-pronged bronze mandrel dripping with dark oil. \"Help me unlace my shirt, Mara.\""
}

