  "text": "Above them, another link in the primary drive-chain sheared with a report like a cannon shot, showering the mercury pool with white-hot sparks that hissed and skittered across the silver surface without sinking. The limp rubber of Vesper’s air-umbilical twitched against the grating.\n\n\"If you unseat the Datum gear from my chest to put it on the spindle, my pallets will lock,\" Kael chirped in the thin heliox, his ribs heaving around the ticking brass housing. \"My heart stops before the wheel ever touches the mandrel.\"\n\n\"Not if the maintaining-power spring takes the load first,\" Mara said. \n\nShe unlatched the floor grating, dropped to her knees on the oily iron ribs, and plunged her right arm up to the shoulder into the mercury. The liquid metal didn't wet her skin; it crushed inward like freezing lead, buoyant and fiercely resisting her push, forcing her sleeve flat against her forearm with terrifying hydrostatic pressure. Her fingertips found the submerged lignum-vitae lever. Bracing her boots against the pontoon truss, she hauled upward.\n\nDeep beneath the quicksilver bath, a secondary bronze barrel groaned awake. Two long, jointed arms—shaped like the hind legs of a grasshopper—rose dripping beads of mercury through the floor-slats and engaged the underside of the Zero-Spindle.\n\n\"Hold still,\" Mara panted, dragging her numbed, silver-streaked arm from the bath. \"The auxiliary train is carrying the escapement throw for ninety seconds. Your chest-housing has a secondary ratchet—Grandfather built the same one into the mantelpiece regulator so he could clean the chime-train while it ran. Kael, give me your calipers.\""
