  "instructions_for_next_hop": "Increment 'hop' by 1. Replace 'text' with the next ~250-word installment of the story (keep 'text' around 250 words total, updating 'summary_so_far' and 'story_bible' to retain memory across the 100 hops). Output ONLY valid JSON.",
  "text": "The rhythmic *clack-clack* of the brass pantograph slowed to a laboured, grinding groan. Across the pool, the great bronze scaffolding—with its familiar, ghostly angles of her grandfather’s stilts-house—sank six inches deeper into the quicksilver bath. A heavy silver wave lapped over the lip of the iron basin, shattering into millions of mirror-bright globules that hissed across the hot floor plates.\n\nIn the slotted rack, the phosphor-bronze stylus was only halfway down the second plate of the Dry Lease. As the five-ton Dredge dragged on the chain-well above, the Zero-Spindle began to shudder, threatening to spin backward.\n\nKael arched his back, his fingers clawing at the grating as the pantograph yoke transmitted the stalling torque directly into his ribcage. Inside his open sternum, the tiny sapphire pallets shrieked against the escape wheel, throwing off microscopic sparks of blue-white fire.\n\n*\"He cannot hold the back-weight!\"* Mara shouted into the brass speaking-cone, her voice high and reedy in the helium mix. *\"The spindle is seizing!\"*\n\n*\"Don't touch the clutch!\"* Vesper’s reply rattled back through the pipe, accompanied by the dull, rhythmic clanging of the fouled chain outside his flooded porthole. *\"If the stylus lifts off the second plate, the lease resets to zero! Look beneath the catwalk—by the keel-beam of the float! There’s a cast-iron sluice wheel marked in red lead!\"*\n\nMara dropped to her belly, squinting through the iron mesh. Three feet below, half-submerged in the trembling mirror of the mercury pool, a spoked wheel jutted from the central pontoon.\n\n*\"I see it!\"*\n\n*\"Blow the trim tanks!\"* Vesper rasped. *\"Drop the reserve quicksilver into the lower sump! If the float rises, the buoyancy will out-pull their winch!\"*"
}

