  "instructions_for_next_hop": "Increment 'hop' by 1. Replace 'text' with the next ~250-word installment of the story (keep 'text' around 250 words total, updating 'summary_so_far' and 'story_bible' to retain memory across the 100 hops). Output ONLY valid JSON.",
  "text": "Mara hooked her knees around the rusted flange of the catwalk and hung upside down over the basin. Her braids brushed the quicksilver, the heavy metal dimpling like warm tallow without wetting a single hair. When she plunged her forearms in to seize the red-lead spokes, the dense liquid shoved her wrists upward with a terrifying, muscular buoyancy, squeezing the blood from her fingers like a vise.\n\nAbove her, Kael gasped—a thin, metallic whistle in the twelve-bar gas. A single tooth on the 62-pin Datum gear slipped a fraction of a millimeter, shaving a curl of bright gold from the Zero-Spindle.\n\nMara braced her boot against the iron curb and hauled. Corrosion shrieked inside the packing gland. With a sudden, hollow *thump*, the cast-iron sluice broke free. She spun it three full turns until the stem hit its brass stop.\n\nDeep beneath the bath, the dump-valves yawned open. Forty tons of ballast mercury roared down the sump-chutes into the abyssal rock, and the displaced silver in the basin surged inward. Freed of its internal weight, the monumental bronze scaffolding—every cross-brace and gable echoing the drowned geometry of her grandfather’s stilts-house—leapt upward two full feet on the dense, gleaming tide.\n\nThe massive bull-gears bit hard. On the rack, the phosphor-bronze stylus tore down the remainder of the second plate and clicked cleanly into the grooves of the third.\n\nAt the end of the pantograph yoke, the blue-white sparking in Kael’s chest vanished, settling back into a crisp, rapid *tick-tack-tick*. He slumped to his elbows, sucking in the cold heliox.\n\nFrom the speaking-cone came a sharp, ringing *ping*, followed by Vesper’s tinny voice: *\"The counterweight’s moving! You’re dragging their Dredge backward up the shaft!\"*"
}

