  "instructions_for_next_hop": "Increment 'hop' by 1. Replace 'text' with the next ~250-word installment of the story (keep 'text' around 250 words total, updating 'summary_so_far' and 'story_bible' to retain memory across the 100 hops). Output ONLY valid JSON.",
  "text": "Mara hauled herself back onto the catwalk, shaking bright, heavy beads of quicksilver from her sleeves. They pattered against the iron grating like buckshot and rolled back into the pool.\n\nBefore her, the bronze scaffolding of the Tide-Engine was no longer struggling; it was racing. Stripped of forty tons of ballast, the float rode high on its mercury mirror, exposing green-verdigrised pilings that had not tasted gas in three centuries. The third phosphor-bronze plate—*Clause VII: The Perpetual Weir*—moved beneath the reading stylus with a shrill, singing whine.\n\n\"Too fast,\" Kael wheezed, his voice pitched like a piccolo in the dense heliox. His fingers, bound in their brass Vernier splints, clutched the edge of his open sternum. Inside his ribcage, the balance wheel was a blur of pale gold, his heartbeat hammered into a frantic, mechanical flutter by the pantograph yoke. \"The float has no drag left. When the stylus clears the final groove, the spindle will freewheel. It’ll strip my escapement to filings.\"\n\nBefore Mara could reach for the yoke’s release pin, the speaking-cone rattled against its bracket.\n\n*\"Hold on!\"* Vesper’s tinny voice crackled through the horn, accompanied by the rhythmic *chuff-chuff* of his revived air-pump. *\"The Registry didn't cut their cable! They’ve wedged the Dredge's flukes into the granite collar at two-eighty! The main chain’s bar-tight!\"*\n\nA deep, sub-audible groan vibrated up through the soles of Mara’s boots. Six hundred feet above them, five tons of hooked iron had snagged fast in the shaft, while down in the cavern, forty tons of buoyant thrust refused to stop rising. On the Zero-Spindle, the last three inches of the third plate fed toward the diamond tip."
