  "text": "The two forces met across two hundred fathoms of hand-forged iron.\n\nIn the center of the mercury pool, the massive bronze scaffolding shuddered as the slack ran out of the main chain. The rising float hit the snagged line like a whale striking the end of a harpoon rope. Mercury erupted around the verdigrised pilings in a sluggish, silver crown that hung in the dense gas before crashing back in blinding sheets.\n\nOn the Zero-Spindle, the diamond stylus shrieked down the last inch of *Clause VII*. Two teeth remained on the sixty-two-pin Datum gear. If the chain held, the spindle would stall half a millimeter short of the ratification notch; if the chain parted, the Sudden Release would spin Kael’s chest mechanism at ten thousand revolutions a minute.\n\n\"Your hand!\" Mara squeaked in the helium-thin air.\n\nShe didn't reach for the jammed release pin. Instead, she seized Kael’s left wrist and drove the hardened brass jaw of his splinted Vernier caliper directly into the teeth of the pantograph’s bevel coupler—waiting until the diamond tip dropped with a heavy, resonant *clack* into the final ratification groove.\n\nSimultaneously, six hundred feet overhead, a sound like a cannon shot echoed down the flooded well. The Registry's anchor-chain had parted.\n\nFreed of five tons of iron, the Tide-Engine lurched skyward. The Zero-Spindle spun into a howling blur. The Vernier splint sheared clean through with a bright shower of sparks, kicking Kael backward onto the grating with his sternum ticking intact—just as Vesper’s voice screamed from the horn: *\"Chain’s coming down the well!\"*"
