  "instructions_for_next_hop": "Increment 'hop' by 1. Replace 'text' with the next ~250-word installment of the story (keep 'text' around 250 words total, updating 'summary_so_far' and 'story_bible' to retain memory across the 100 hops). Output ONLY valid JSON.",
  "text": "Beads of liquid silver hissed across the iron grating, rolling like frantic beetles toward the edge. Mara threw an arm over her eyes as link after eighty-pound link piled into the central basin. Because the mercury was thirteen times denser than water, the iron did not sink to the bottom of the vat; it floated in a writhing, semi-submerged reef, building a jagged spire of black chain up through the center of the scaffolding.\n\n*\"Brace!\"* Kael’s helium-thinned shout cracked in the dense air.\n\nHe dragged her behind one of the main bronze standards just as the five-ton Dredge—and the shattered remains of the Third Counterweight—hit the narrow throat of the shaft ninety fathoms above the cavern roof.\n\nThe impact didn't reach the mercury pool. Instead, the falling mass wedged straight into the choked bird’s-nest of chain backing up the vertical well. The shockwave traveled down the tangled links, a deafening *clack-clack-clack* that set the mercury churning in slow, heavy swells. Red rust and pulverized basalt rained from the shaft mouth.\n\nFrom the brass horn on the pillar came the sound of tearing metal, followed by a high, whistling hiss.\n\n*\"The Dredge hung up at four-ten!\"* Vesper wheezed, his voice echoing inside his copper helmet. *\"It’s kicked the shaft liner sideways into my manifold! The bulkhead’s bowing—I can hear rivets popping like pistol shots! Girl, that little steel arbor you wedged in the outer hatch is bending like a willow twig!\"*\n\nKael gripped the service ladder bolted inside the northern piling. Because the scaffolding had risen to the roof, the ladder’s top rungs now aligned directly with the service spiral leading up to four hundred fathoms."
