  "text": "The rhythmic *clank* stopped, replaced by the shrill, pressurized shriek of a blow-down valve venting into the twelve-bar shaft. \n\nMara dropped the copper helmet and crept to the manifold room’s open hatchway, peering down through the iron grating of the four-hundred-fathom landing. Ten fathoms below, wedged diagonally in the jagged mountain of broken counterweight chain, the rusted iron cylinder she had mistaken for a solid ballast weight was splitting along a vertical seam. Pale yellow light spilled from its belly, illuminating the drifting fog with a greasy halo.\n\n*\"Bailiffs,\"* Kael breathed beside her, his sea-glass eyes narrowing as two bulky figures in articulated cast-iron suits lumbered out onto the tangled links. Their joints hissed with hydraulic oil, and each carried a long copper cylinder strapped to his back, feeding a braided hose to a brass rod in his pincer-gauntlet. *\"One-bar hard-suits. They didn't even have to equalize.\"* \n\nOne of the armored giants struck his rod against a chain link. A blinding, violet-white spark flared, instantly slicing through four inches of forged steel like warm tallow. Molten slag pattered down toward the dark Nave below.\n\n*\"Magnesium lances,\"* Vesper squeaked behind them, hobbling to the doorway on legs stiff from eighty years in cold brine. The lead sinkers in his beard clicked against his brass collar. *\"They aren't coming up for us. They're going down to the Nave ceiling. If they burn through the four bronze pawls holding up the Zero-Spindle scaffolding, the whole rig drops back into the sump and the basalt sluices slam shut.\"* \n\nHe seized Mara’s shoulder with a cold, taloned hand and pointed his spanner toward a narrow brass hatch behind the manifold pipes, stenciled with a faded red arrow: *VENTURI CHUTE — TRIM TANK B.*"
