  "text": "The copper flume leveled out in a spray of dried tallow flakes, spitting Kael and Mara onto a grated catwalk that hummed like a plucked bass string. Beneath their boots, the entire vault of Archive Zero roared with the sub-audible thunder of the open sluices drinking the upper sea.\n\nThey were in the upper pawl-gallery. Four bronze ratchets, each the size of a dory, bit deep into the corner-posts of the Zero-Spindle scaffolding, holding its massive weight suspended above the mercury pool fifteen fathoms below. \n\nVesper was already at the rail, his lead-braided beard swinging as he fitted his spanner to a swivel-mounted brass nozzle connected to the basalt wall by a braided copper hose. *\"Trim Tank B still holds forty-bar head pressure from the outer trench!\"* the old man squeaked through the dense helium. *\"Kael, take the elevation wheel—my fingers won't close on the spokes!\"*\n\nAbove them, the tangled jungle of severed anchor-chain hanging in the central shaft groaned. Two massive shapes dropped out of the twelve-bar fog, arrested by twin steel winch-cables. They landed on the scaffolding roof with a dull, monumental *clang* that shook rust from the ceiling ribs.\n\nThe Registry Bailiffs stood seven feet tall in cast-iron shells painted primer-red, their domed helmets studded with thick quartz bullseyes. Neither looked toward the gallery. Moving with slow, hydraulic certainty, the lead Bailiff knelt beside the northeast pawl, snapped a glass ampoule against his iron knee, and touched it to the tip of a six-foot iron pipe. \n\nA blinding, blue-white star of burning magnesium ignited in the fog, showering the bronze ratchet in molten sparks."
