  "text": "The actinic glare carved sharp, violet shadows across the twelve-bar mist. Thick gouts of liquefied bronze dripped from the northeast pawl, hissing as they struck the damp iron plates of the scaffolding roof.\n\nKael slammed his good shoulder into the elevation wheel, his chest-escapement clicking at a frantic, hammering tempo. Mara threw her weight beside him, her boots skidding on tallow-grease as they brought the long brass nozzle to bear on the kneeling giant.\n\n*\"Open the gate!\"* Kael chirped.\n\nVesper dropped his full weight onto the three-foot bronze spanner. The seized valve shrieked, shedding a crust of green verdigris, and gave way.\n\nThe braided copper hose stiffened like a struck serpent. A solid, white-hot rod of forty-bar abyssal brine erupted from the nozzle with a deafening, hydraulic tear. In the dense heliox, the jet didn't spray; it travelled across the thirty-foot gap as a coherent lance of black water, striking the kneeling Bailiff squarely in his cast-iron shoulder.\n\nThe impact rang like a sledgehammer against an anvil. The two-ton suit skidded backward across the wet plates, tearing the magnesium pipe from the Bailiff's articulated pincer, and toppled over the edge of the scaffolding. His winch-cable snapped taut ten feet below the roof, swinging him like a pendulum above the mirror-bright mercury pool. \n\nYet the severed lance remained wedged in the northeast pawl, burning furiously through the last inch of bronze.\n\nWorse, the second Bailiff did not ignite his pipe on the northwest ratchet. He turned his quartz bullseyes toward the gallery, raised the six-foot magnesium lance like a harpoon, and stepped toward the catwalk rail—just as a blister of rotted copper bulged on their supply hose."
