  "text": "The catwalk groaned beneath the Bailiff’s two-ton tread, rivets popping like pistol shots into the violet haze. The iron giant lunged, his right pincer snapping shut an inch from Kael’s throat with a deafening clang that showered them in dried whale-oil tallow.\n\n*\"His joints are packed against twelve-bar!\"* Vesper piped, his milky eyes wide as he swung the heavy bronze spanner in a stiff, two-handed arc. The tool bounced off the Bailiff’s bulbous cuirass with a dull *thwack*, leaving only a bright smear of brass on the pig-iron. *\"Break the packing! Let the Nave in!\"*\n\nThe Bailiff backhanded Vesper, sending the ancient keeper skidding across the brine-slick grating until his braided lead beard tangled in the sheared stanchion. The suit pivoted back toward Kael, its steam-boiler hissing through a dorsal condenser, raising both hydraulic claws to crush the boy against the dead cannon.\n\nMara didn’t look at the pincers; she looked at the accordion-pleated leather gaiters shielding the giant’s left knee-joint, where a brass grease-nipple protruded between overlapping iron segments. \n\nShe dove beneath the sweep of the steel elbow, smelling hot tallow and scorching asbestos. With both hands, she drove the tapered steel point of Hollis’s bent clock-arbor straight into the leather pleat behind the knee, twisting it hard behind the grease-nipple as the Bailiff stepped forward.\n\nThe servo-ratchet chewed into the hardened clock-steel and jammed. The giant’s left leg locked mid-stride. Off-balance on the canted deck, the two-ton suit pitched forward onto one knee, its quartz bullseye level with Kael’s ticking chest."
