nging it to one knee.",
  "instructions_for_next_hop": "Increment 'hop' by 1. Replace 'text' with the next ~250-word installment of the story (keep 'text' around 250 words total, updating 'summary_so_far' and 'story_bible' to retain memory across the 100 hops). Output ONLY valid JSON.",
  "text": "Through the four-inch quartz bullseye, Mara glimpsed a pale, sweating face framed by speaking-tubes and brass gauges. The Bailiff’s left pincer swept down to crush her against the grating, hydraulic fluid weeping from its overtaxed elbow.\n\nKael didn't retreat. He lunged forward onto the giant’s bowed iron shoulder, bracing his bare feet against the riveted collar-ring. With his bleeding left hand, he jammed the jagged remnant of his shattered brass Vernier caliper under the copper-mesh shroud of the dorsal exhaust valve. \n\n*\"Vesper!\"* Kael chirped, his voice a high, reedy whistle in the helium-rich air. *\"The relief cock! Strike it inward!\"*\n\nVesper tore his lead-braided beard free of the stanchion, leaving gray hairs twisted in the jagged bronze. He scrambled up the 15-degree slope and swung the four-foot bronze spanner like a sledgehammer. The heavy jaws struck the spring-loaded check-valve behind the Bailiff's neck.\n\nBrass threads sheared. Instead of one-bar boiler steam venting out, twelve atmospheres of dense, icy heliox slammed *inward* through the two-inch breach like a solid iron rod.\n\nThe sound wasn't an explosion, but a terrifying, muffled *thump*—a reverse thunderclap that sucked the fog from the catwalk in a sudden vortex. Inside the pig-iron shell, the pressure differential hit the operator at twelve tons per square foot. The quartz bullseye crazed into opaque white frost and spiderwebbed inward, instantly smeared with dark crimson. \n\nThe hydraulic pincers went slack, clattering against the iron grating. The two-ton suit froze, kneeling like an iron penitent before the dead brine cannon, its dorsal pipe whistling a thin, fading note as the pressure equalized."
