  "text": "The thin whistle of equalizing heliox died in the Bailiff's dorsal pipe, leaving only the deep, hydraulic roar of the basalt sluices vibrating through the sole of Mara's boots. Then the iron grating beneath them groaned—a sharp, crystalline *ping* of overstressed bronze.\n\n*\"The southeast pawl!\"* Vesper squeaked, his milky eyes wide as he pressed an ear to the canted stanchion. *\"Two tons of dead pig-iron on the overhang! The tooth is fissuring!\"*\n\nAbove the fog bank, a heavy winch drum clanked inside the Knuckle-Bell. The steel umbilical cable hooked between the dead Bailiff’s shoulder blades jerked taut. It didn't lift the suit; instead, the Dredge was angling away, dragging the two-ton corpse sideways against the guardrail like a grappling hook to tear the gallery loose.\n\nThe whole scaffolding shuddered, listing another degree toward the black mirror of the mercury lake fifteen fathoms below. \n\nMara scrambled around the kneeling iron tomb. The magnesium lance still lay wedged in the suit’s slack right pincer, its copper oxygen-feed tube hissing faintly. She wrenched the heavy bronze rod free, braced its butt against her hip, and twisted the flint-wheel igniter at the breech.\n\nA blinding, blue-white sun erupted on the catwalk, banishing the tallow-smelling fog. Shielding her eyes with her blistered forearm, Mara pressed the spitting tip against the braided steel winch cable just above the Bailiff's dorsal shackle.\n\nMolten steel rained in a shower of white sparks that bounced harmlessly off the iron grating. Above them, the Knuckle-Bell's engines revved, hauling harder."
}

