  "text": "Kael scrambled after her, the braided copper hose trailing between them as the lance spat blinding white sparks across the wet bronze trusses. \n\nInside the Knuckle-Bell, a pale face pressed against the thick quartz bull’s-eye port—a Registry winchman in a woollen cap, eyes wide behind the four-inch glass. Above the sphere’s crown, the two-inch braided steel hoist-cable abruptly snapped taut. Grease smoked from the top sheave as the distant surface engines at Spire Four engaged, trying to haul the five-ton hull back up into the fog.\n\nInstead of lifting clean, the Dredge’s iron skids caught beneath the lip of the Zero-Spindle’s outer rib. The scaffolding groaned. Behind them, the cracked southeast pawl let out a sharp, crystalline *ping* as the upward pull twisted the entire frame in its ceiling sockets.\n\n*\"They’re tearing the roof off!\"* Vesper piped, bracing himself against the brine monitor.\n\nMara braced her boot against the Dredge’s riveted skirt. *\"Hold the slack, Kael!\"* \n\nShe jammed the sputtering magnesium rod directly against the taut, grease-slicked hoist-cable just above the clevis pin. The twelve-bar atmosphere compressed the flame into a screaming white needle. Braided steel wires parted like plucked harp-strings—*spang, spang, spang*—whipping through the tallow-mist and gouging deep bright scores into the iron shell.\n\nThe oxygen flask on Kael’s hip gave a hollow, dying wheeze. The glare shrank to a dull orange ember just as the final core-strand melted through.\n\nThe severed cable shot skyward into the dark like a struck viper. Untethered, the five-ton Knuckle-Bell settled heavily back against the bent guardrail stanchions, teetering over the fifteen-fathom drop to the mercury lake."
