  "text": "Through the thick quartz bull’s-eye, the winchman saw the bronze spanner bite into the external bleed-cock. He lunged forward, slamming a grease-stained palm against the glass, his mouth stretched wide in a silent plea. \n\nMara tapped two fingers against her nose and mimed blowing against pinched nostrils. *Clear your ears,* she mouthed.\n\nVesper leaned his skeletal weight onto the spanner. The brass cap shrieked as its painted seal broke, and then the valve stem turned a quarter-inch. \n\nA thin, ear-splitting whistle tore through the gallery as the twelve-bar heliox atmosphere of the Nave forced its way through the quarter-inch bore into the one-bar sphere. Inside the Knuckle-Bell, the air instantly flashed into a violent, adiabatic haze—compression heating the cramped cabin like the cylinder of a diesel engine. Through the swirling fog behind the quartz, Mara saw the winchman drop to his knees, clutching his temples as the pressure slammed against his tympanic membranes, before he desperately pinched his nose and convulsed, swallowing hard.\n\n*\"Don't strip the threads,\"* Kael rasped, his good hand steadying the trembling iron curve of the bell’s skirt while his bandaged left hand dripped dark blood onto the grated catwalk. Down in the black nave below them, a dull, rhythmic *thud-thud-thud* began to vibrate through the iron pillars—the first bubbles of twelve-bar gas burping upward through the thinning water column of the four-hundred-fathom moon pool.\n\n*\"The seal is lifting,\"* Mara said, her duck-quack voice tight. *\"The water head is dropping too fast.\"* \n\nThe whistle died to a hoarse hiss as the pressure inside the iron sphere equalized with the gallery. Without waiting for the fog inside to clear, Kael grabbed the heavy iron dog-wheel on the Dredge’s ventral skirt and wrenched it counter-clockwise."
