  "text": "The ventral plug swung inward with a greasy thump, releasing a wave of roasting-hot air that smelled of scorched whale-oil and singed wool. \n\nKael hauled himself up through the circular coaming first, his chest-gears clicking rapidly against the iron rim. Inside, the spherical cabin was scarcely six feet across, lined with brass pressure-gauges, copper accumulator tubes, and three heavy hydraulic levers. The pinch-faced winchman lay curled on the slatted floorboards beneath the control quadrant, twin threads of bright blood leaking from his ears, giggling high and thin in the grip of acute pressure-narcosis.\n\n*\"Get the Dry Lease plates in!\"* Kael quacked down through the hole, shoving the delirious winchman aside with his boot.\n\nMara passed the leather satchel containing the three phosphor-bronze plates up into Kael's good hand, then boosted Vesper’s bony knees until the old Bell-Ringer tumbled over the coaming, lead beard-weights clattering against the iron hull. \n\nBelow them, the entire cathedral of Archive Zero groaned. A massive bubble of twelve-bar heliox—twenty feet across—erupted upward through the moon pool shaft at four hundred fathoms, carrying a geyser of black water that smashed against the underside of the scaffolding and showered the pawl-gallery in freezing spray. The atmospheric pressure in the Nave dropped half a bar in a single second; instantly, the air around Mara turned white with condensation fog.\n\n*\"Mara, inside!\"* Kael shouted, leaning out of the hatch into the blinding mist.\n\n*\"If we seal the hatch now, we still weigh nine tons!\"* Mara cried back, gripping the heavy bronze spanner Vesper had left on the catwalk. She ducked beneath the curving belly of the sphere, where her grandfather’s bent steel clock-arbor remained wedged in the keel clevis, holding the five-ton cast-iron ballast shoe fast."
