  "text": "The heavy iron plug slammed into its seat with a greased thud, cutting off the banshee shriek of the decompressing Nave. Mara rolled onto her back on the curved steel grating, kicking the central dogging-wheel until the four steel wedges bit home. Around the rim, the gutta-percha gasket hissed, spat a thin froth of oil, and sealed—trapping twelve atmospheres of dense heliox inside the eight-foot bronze shell.\n\nAbove them, the three hydraulic grapple-claws groaned against the roof ribs as the pressure outside the hull dropped another three bars in a single heartbeat. \n\n*\"Hold the stays!\"* Kael’s voice piped shrill and metallic in the single lantern’s amber glare. He wedged his boots against the unconscious Winchman’s chest, pinning the three phosphor-bronze plates of the Dry Lease beneath his knees, and reached up with his good right hand to yank the red brass bleed-lever on the overhead manifold.\n\nHot castor oil sprayed across the curved wall. Outside the four-inch quartz bullseyes, the three bronze claws snapped open.\n\nFor half a second the Knuckle-Bell hung weightless in the screaming white gale of the upper gallery. Then the gale caught it. The five-ton sphere lurched sidewise, sheared a cast-iron pawl-stanchion clean off its rivets with a deafening *boom*, and was sucked straight down and sideways into the upturned lip of the four-hundred-fathom moon pool.\n\nWater and expanding gas hit the hull like a battering ram. The lantern shattered. In pitch blackness, amidst the steady, frantic *tick-tick-tick* of the 62-pin Datum gear inside Kael’s ribs, the buoyant bronze bell shot skyward through the boiling throat of the shaft."
