  "text": "Twenty fathoms. Ten. Through the weeping quartz bullseye, the black water paled to bottle-green, then exploded into froth.\n\nThe Knuckle-Bell breached the moon pool like a cast-iron whale. For two heartbeats of weightlessness, Mara floated off the greasy floorboards, her shoulders bumping Vesper’s lead-braided beard while the phosphor-bronze Lease plates hung suspended in the dense air. Outside the viewport flashed the high, smoke-blackened rafters of Spire Four’s gantry hall.\n\nThen the five-ton sphere arced sideways, smashed through the timber safety railings, and slammed onto the iron decking. \n\nThey tumbled in a heap of bruised limbs, bilge water, and clattering brass. The bell rolled half a turn, grinding across riveted floor-plates before wedging fast against the base of the great steam-winch. \n\nSilence followed, broken only by the steady, rapid *tick-tick-tick* of Kael’s sternum and a sharp, metallic *ping* from the belly hatch.\n\nA bolt head ricocheted off the curved ceiling, sparking against the bronze.\n\n*\"Reverse pressure!\"* Vesper’s helium-warped voice was a reed whistling in a gale. He pointed a trembling, pale finger at the lower hatch. *\"The dogs are bevelled for sea-weight, not inner wind! Twelve atmospheres will pop that lid like a champagne cork—and boil our blood in the throat!\"*\n\nAround the hatch rim, the tallow-soaked hemp gasket was already extruding outward like pale worms, hissing violently as the twelve-bar heliox forced its way into the one-bar surface air. \n\nKael dragged himself to the viewport, smearing blood from his linen-wrapped hand across the quartz. *\"The Registry’s saturation lock is ten feet left!\"* he piped. *\"If we use the hydraulic knuckle-arm to drag us to the mating flange, we can clamp the collar before the bolts shear!\"*"
